## 0. Verdict

PASS

`lsp_comp_take` already refuses `list_len(out) >= 64`.
The catalog is 30 fixed `lsp_comp_take` calls. There is no catalog while.
Empty source and a 0-byte file yield prefix `""`. That returns the 30 items.
A huge prefix matches no label. The walk is still 30 takes.
No new long-lived buffer. MEM did not edit product files.

## 1. Bound already on disk

  File: `cli/lsp_complete.oo`. 179 lines. Header beat 4 names the cap.

    fn lsp_comp_take(...) -> List[String] {
        if list_len(out) >= 64 {
            return out;
        }
        if str_starts_with(label, prefix) {
            return list_push(out, lsp_comp_item(...));
        }
        return out;
    }

  Check is before `list_push`. Max length is 64.
  Catalog today is 30 labels. Cap is defensive.
  HARN named the same cap in `audit/plan1_harn.oot`.

  User order: if no bound, add a 64-item cap.
  Bound is present. MEM added none.

## 2. Catalog build cannot loop

  `lsp_complete_result` is a straight-line list of 30 takes:

    9 caps, 13 keywords, 5 types, 3 builtins.

  There is no while over a catalog string. There is no recursive resolve.
  `list_push` exists only inside `lsp_comp_take`.

  Other loops in this file:

  | site | guard | progress | bound |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `lsp_comp_uri` | `i < n` | `i = i + 1` | `n = chars_len(body)` |
  | `lsp_comp_prefix` | `start > 0` | `start = start - 1` or `break` | `start` falls to 0 |
  | `lsp_comp_join` | `i < n` | `i = i + 1` | `n = list_len(items) <= 64` |

  Shared read-only helpers in `cli/lsp_ident.oo` also progress:

  | site | bound |
  | --- | --- |
  | `lsp_json_int` | `i < n`, increment or break |
  | `lsp_src_offset` | `i < n` and line or col, `i` increments |
  | `lsp_ident_at` | `a` decreases; `b` increases to `n` |

  A huge `"line"` or `"character"` still walks at most `chars_len(src)`.
  MEM did not edit `cli/lsp_ident.oo`.

## 3. Empty file and 0-byte file

  `lsp_comp_load` returns `""` when the URI is missing, contains `..`,
  does not exist, or `read_file` fails. A real 0-byte file is also `""`.

  On `src == ""`:
    `lsp_src_offset` sees `n == 0` and returns 0.
    `lsp_ident_at` sees `n <= 0` and returns `""`.
    `lsp_comp_prefix` keeps `start == 0` and returns `""`.

  `oo_str_starts_with` returns true when `pre.len <= 0`
  (`runtime/chs_rt_str_ops.c`). Empty prefix matches every label.
  Thirty takes push 30 items. 30 < 64. Join walks 30.
  That is the catalog. It is not a hang. It is not a crash.

## 4. Huge prefix

  Prefix is the ident under the cursor, plus `&` when the previous
  character is `&`. It is a slice of `src`. It is not a JSON `"prefix"` key.

  If the ident is longer than every label, `str_starts_with` is false
  (`pre.len > s.len` returns 0). Zero pushes. Join emits
  `{"isIncomplete":false,"items":[]}`.

  Filter cost is 30 starts_with calls. It does not walk the prefix
  as a catalog. It does not grow the list.

## 5. No new long-lived buffers

  `out` is `list_new()` inside `lsp_complete_result`. It dies with the call.
  Join `buf` is a local string. `src` is a per-request `read_file`, same
  as hover. There is no static list. There is no module `mut`. There is
  no catalog cache file. There is no `process_exec`.

  `isIncomplete` is the literal `false`. The server does not keep a
  remainder list for a later resolve.

